{"id":"n-20261027-kwhgss","category":"sports","display_title":"Brewers Crush Rays in Game 3","display_title_he":"הברוורס הביסו את הרייס במשחק 3","short_summary":"The Milwaukee Brewers defeated the Tampa Bay Rays 10-1 to claim a 3-0 lead in the World Series, standing just one win away from their first championship.","english_level":"C1","words":482,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/26/brewers-rays-world-series-game-3-baseball","title":"Ruthless Brewers close in on World Series sweep after crushing Rays 10-1 in Game 3","published_at":"2026-10-27T03:22:00.000Z"},{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/27/nx-s1-6019094/mlb-world-series-tuesday","title":"Brewers rout the Rays 10-1 to move within a win of their first World Series title","published_at":"2026-10-27T05:45:44.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-27T03:22:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:07.824Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Milwaukee Brewers moved to the brink of history on Monday night by crushing the Tampa Bay Rays 10-1 at Tropicana Field. Taking a commanding three-game lead in the best-of-seven championship series, the Brewers now stand just one victory away from capturing the first World Series title in franchise history. Their dominant performance was anchored by an exceptional outing from rookie left-hander Robert Gasser, alongside a historic offensive explosion driven by the team's young core, placing them on the verge of ending a decades-long championship drought.","Gasser delivered a stellar pitching performance, allowing only a single line-drive hit to Yandy Díaz while facing the absolute minimum number of batters through six innings. With the assistance of a caught stealing and a double play, he became the first starting pitcher to face the minimum eighteen batters through six innings of a World Series game since Curt Schilling in 2001, and the first left-hander to achieve the feat since Sandy Koufax for the Los Angeles Dodgers in 1965. Despite playing in a hostile environment at the quirky, cavernous stadium whose roof was previously shredded by Hurricane Milton, Gasser acknowledged the vocal backing of twenty thousand traveling fans who cheered loudly from behind the visitors' dugout.","While Gasser locked down opposing hitters on the mound, Milwaukee's lineup broke the game wide open during a remarkable fifth inning. The Brewers plated eight runs in a single frame, setting a postseason record by stringing together seven consecutive hits with two outs. Outfielder Jackson Chourio initiated the relentless rally with a single and later stole second base, while teammate Brice Turang provided a crucial two-run single that slipped past shortstop Taylor Walls' glove. Contributions from William Contreras, Garrett Mitchell, Cooper Pratt, Sal Frelick, and David Hamilton quickly turned the contest into a rout as the team accumulated sixteen hits against Freddy Peralta and five relievers.","Chourio finished the night four for five at the plate, cementing a stellar postseason run. At twenty-two years old, his impressive multi-hit performance and stolen base placed him second only to Ty Cobb in 1908 as the youngest player to achieve those combined statistics in a World Series game. Brewers manager Pat Murphy praised the young player's remarkable discipline, comparing his competitive focus to late basketball legend Kobe Bryant.","On the other side, the Tampa Bay Rays struggled to find momentum after leading the American League with ninety-eight wins during the regular season. Pitcher Freddy Peralta faced difficulties against his former team, allowing five runs and seven hits before exiting in the fifth inning. Although passionate home fans filled the sellout crowd, uncharacteristic defensive mistakes and offensive stagnation left the Rays facing a daunting three-game deficit. Historical statistics heavily favor Milwaukee, as only one team in postseason history—the 2004 Boston Red Sox—has ever successfully rebounded from a three-to-zero series deficit. The Brewers will look to complete the sweep under manager Pat Murphy during Game 4."],"facts":[{"fact":"The Milwaukee Brewers defeated the Tampa Bay Rays 10-1 in Game 3 of the World Series.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Milwaukee took a 3-0 lead in the best-of-seven series, moving within one victory of their first World Series title.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Rookie left-hander Robert Gasser pitched one-hit ball and faced the minimum 18 batters through six innings.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The Brewers scored eight runs in the fifth inning with a postseason-record seven straight hits with two outs.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Jackson Chourio went 4-for-5 with a stolen base, becoming the second-youngest player with four hits and a stolen base in a World Series game.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Milwaukee","lemma":"Milwaukee","pos":"noun","he":"מילווקי","name":true},{"text":"Brewers","lemma":"Brewers","pos":"noun","he":"הברוארס","name":true},{"text":"moved","lemma":"move","pos":"verb","he":"התקדם","name":false},{"text":"brink","lemma":"brink","pos":"noun","he":"סף","name":false},{"text":"history","lemma":"history","pos":"noun","he":"היסטוריה","name":false},{"text":"Monday","lemma":"Monday","pos":"noun","he":"יום שני","name":true},{"text":"night","lemma":"night","pos":"noun","he":"לילה","name":false},{"text":"crushing","lemma":"crush","pos":"verb","he":"למחץ","name":false},{"text":"Tampa Bay","lemma":"Tampa Bay","pos":"noun","he":"טמפה ביי","name":true},{"text":"Rays","lemma":"Rays","pos":"noun","he":"הריז","name":true},{"text":"Tropicana Field","lemma":"Tropicana Field","pos":"noun","he":"טרופיקנה פילד","name":true},{"text":"commanding","lemma":"commanding","pos":"adjective","he":"שליט / בולט","name":false},{"text":"three-game","lemma":"three